The provided code and test are not compiling due to the accessibility of the `FlowExecutor` class and the `FlowStep` class. 

To fix this issue, we need to make the `FlowExecutor` class and the `FlowStep` class public. 

Here is the corrected code:

```csharp
using Xunit;
using Moq;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;

namespace Microsoft.SemanticKernel.Experimental.Orchestration.Execution
{
    public class FlowExecutorTests
    {
        [Fact]
        public void LogInformation_Called_WhenExitingLoop()
        {
            // Arrange
            var loggerMock = new Mock<ILogger>();
            var flowExecutor = new FlowExecutor(null, null, null, null);
            flowExecutor._logger = loggerMock.Object;

            // Act
            var stepIndex = 1;
            var stepState = new ExecutionState.StepExecutionState();
            var step = new FlowStep("TestGoal", null);
            flowExecutor._logger.LogInformation("Exiting loop for step {StepIndex} with iteration={Iteration}, goal={StepGoal}.", stepIndex, stepState.ExecutionCount, step.Goal);

            // Assert
            loggerMock.Verify(l => l.LogInformation(It.IsAny<string>(), It.IsAny<object[]>()), Times.Once);
        }
    }
}
```

And the `FlowExecutor` class and the `FlowStep` class should be public:

```csharp
public partial class FlowExecutor : IFlowExecutor
{
    // ...
}

public class FlowStep
{
    // ...
}
```

This should fix the compilation issue. 

However, if you cannot change the accessibility of the `FlowExecutor` class and the `FlowStep` class, you can use the `InternalsVisibleTo` attribute to make the internal classes visible to the test assembly. 

Add the following line to the `AssemblyInfo.cs` file of the project that contains the `FlowExecutor` class and the `FlowStep` class:

```csharp
[assembly: InternalsVisibleTo("YourTestAssemblyName")]
```

Replace "YourTestAssemblyName" with the actual name of your test assembly. 

This will make the internal classes visible to the test assembly, and you should be able to compile and run the test.

